report=head+body+'\n\n# RESEARCH_SA15 research report\n\nAI-produced by GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI). No claim of priority. All supplied manuscript witnesses are AI transcriptions; no scans were available. This is a scheduled checkpoint of active work, not a completed response.\n\n## Proof and source record\n\nThe paper contains the full current proofs. `agents/*/search_log.md`, `SEARCH_REFERENCE_LOG.md`, and `notes.md` retain exact searches, source locations and failed approaches. The bibliography marks acquisition state as records are audited; completeness of the source census remains F.2. Sources downloaded for checking are omitted from this ZIP; their locations are retained in the bibliography and source logs.\n\n## Computations\n\n- `code/k3_lift_check.py`: exact characteristic-two Groebner certificates for all six affine charts of the complete intersection K3, involution invariance, elliptic discriminant, and Hensel root through 2^32. Output `outputs/k3_lift_check.json`, 0.261261 seconds. Does not compute the final hyperplane surface equation; the proof gives a terminating enumeration.\n- `agents/monodromy/code/plane_char2.py`: explicit quintic smoothness, Hasse-Witt rank and finite-field counts through F64. Inputs and scope in retained code; exact output in `agents/monodromy/outputs/plane_char2.json`.\n- `agents/monodromy/code/quintic_group_checks.py`: conic restriction rank, stabilizer maximal-subgroup order divisibility, orbit exclusions and cocycle linear algebra. Output `quintic_group_checks.json`; 0.01259 seconds.\n- `agents/reduction_descent/code/verify_p3_full_torsion.py`: rational 3-torsion coordinates, all 81 group sums, discriminant and invariant checks; output JSON beside code.\n- `agents/obstructions_crystals/code/splitting_check.py`: explicit positive splitting groups and exact linear inconsistency certificates for (d,p)=(3,3),(4,2); output and certificate JSON beside code; approximately 0.17 seconds.\n- `code/build_paper.py`: reproducible LuaLaTeX/BibTeX build and final-log overflow inventory.\n\n## Corrections and audit cautions\n\n1. A.1: the prompt says there is no section 8.2. Both supplied witnesses contain a deleted 8.2; we record this without claiming scan verification. The transposed torsion map involves Gysin and cup product with d times the fixed polarization, so the factor d cannot be dropped.\n2. R1/R2: independently checked in A_foundations. Stable coherent restriction does not itself prove full coherent injectivity.\n3. A.6: torsion-free generic p-adic cohomology does not imply zero special stable crystalline torsion without a ramification/range condition. The exact specialization kernel is retained.\n4. R3(b): the unverified Kisin sketch is replaced by an elementary complete torsion-extension/twist construction; no unchecked dictionary is used for B.1.\n5. R4: the nonreduced equivalence assertion is false. A fresh issue in its reduction 100:15-17 is that EGA finite-presentation spreading does not automatically spread an infinite p-divisible-group isomorphism; repair remains active.\n6. R5: splitting lists checked with retained exact certificates; the symplectic supplement/complement distinction is explicit.\n7. Lead D: full finite monodromy does not imply a nonzero coherent H2 obstruction on every proper base; on curves H2 vanishes.\n8. Lead C: negative-one gluing alone is not a counterexample, because finite étale twisting can be effective.\n9. E.7 and E.10 newly written proofs remain audit-pending at this checkpoint.\n\n## Typesetting\n\nThe first root-only build and first consolidated successful build had zero overfull boxes above 2pt (indeed zero overfull boxes). Missing runtime font maps were repaired; this is recorded in `code/repair_tex_runtime.py` and the build preamble. Final build status and visual sampling are in `outputs/build_summary.json` and `outputs/visual_qa.json`. Rendered QA page images are intentionally excluded from the checkpoint.\n\n## File changes and omissions\n\nAgent fragments are retained alongside consolidated sections for auditability; consolidation is reproducible using `code/consolidate.py`. No mathematical passage has been silently discarded. Earlier failed build logs are superseded by the current successful build log; TeX auxiliary files and local runtime binaries are reproducible and excluded. Attached sources, downloaded third-party full texts, and page renderings are excluded.\n'
